{"content":[{"c":["HIEL"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Bethelite in the days of King Ahab who fulfilled Joshua’s curse upon the city of Jericho (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.6.26","r":"Josh.6.26","rawR":"Josh.6.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.6.26","value":"Josh.6.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 6:26"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.16.34","r":"1Kgs.16.34","rawR":"1Kgs.16.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.16.34","value":"1Kgs.16.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 16:34"},"). Joshua had said centuries before that anyone attempting to rebuild the city would suffer the loss of his oldest and youngest sons. It is unclear whether Hiel’s sons died a natural death or were killed in a punitive ritual."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Hiel","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 6:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.6.26","rawQueryValue":"Josh.6.26","sourceRefExact":"Josh.6.26"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 16:34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.16.34","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.16.34","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.16.34"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"a7f213efcfecfc2a93beebcac63229c4a2ae5e93ee45fac5b919cf05be67152f","sourceItemName":"Hiel","sourceItemOrder":288,"sourceMember":"Articles/H.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Hiel","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Hiel","title":"Hiel","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}